"""Render a portable report from redacted smoke evidence; never reads keys."""
import base64
import html
import json
from pathlib import Path

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
OUT = ROOT / 'qa-results' / 'live-smoke'
accounts = json.loads((OUT / 'results.json').read_text())
native = json.loads((OUT / 'native-results.json').read_text())
images = {}
for account in accounts:
    for name in account['screens']:
        images[name] = 'data:image/png;base64,' + base64.b64encode((OUT / name).read_bytes()).decode()
rows = ''
for a in accounts:
    plans = '; '.join(f"{p['type']} {p.get('pool', '')} · {p['status']}" for p in a['plans']) or 'No supported memberships'
    rows += f"<tr><td>{html.escape(a['account'])}</td><td>{html.escape(plans)}</td><td>{a['usable']}</td><td>{a.get('assignedIps', '—')}</td><td>{'Layout issue' if a.get('layoutErrors') else 'Passed'}</td></tr>"
cards = ''.join(f'<article><h3>{html.escape(k)}</h3><p>{html.escape(v)}</p></article>' for k, v in native.items())
doc = '''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Shifter · Real-account smoke results</title>
<style>body{margin:0;background:#0d1422;color:#e8edf5;font:16px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:36px 24px}h1{font-size:34px;line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:40px;font-size:23px}h3{margin:0;font-size:17px}p{color:#b7c4d8}.tag{color:#77b3ff;font-size:13px}article,.issue{background:#151f31;border:1px solid #2c3a50;border-radius:12px;padding:20px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(245px,1fr));gap:14px}.issue{border-color:#a6793c}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}td,th{text-align:left;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #2c3a50}th{color:#8ea5c8}.scroll{overflow:auto}select{background:#18283f;color:white;border:1px solid #415575;border-radius:6px;padding:10px;margin:0 10px 16px 0}#shot{display:block;max-width:100%;max-height:850px;margin:auto;border:1px solid #2c3a50;border-radius:8px}code{color:#8fbaff}small{color:#a5b4cd}li{margin:10px 0}</style>
<main><div class="tag">LOCAL TEST EXECUTION · REAL BACKEND · 11 OCTOBER 2026</div><h1>Shifter smoke-test results</h1>
<p>Ten supplied accounts authenticated through the app’s actual HTTP adapter. All ten rendered at 320×568, 393×852, 820×1180 and 1440×900 with the shipped fonts and no Flutter layout exceptions. These are widget-rendered sizes; they do not represent forty physical-device tests.</p>
<div class="cards">CARDS</div>
<h2>Two confirmed bugs</h2><div class="issue"><h3>High priority: desktop sign-out throws runtime exceptions</h3><p>Sign in with the paid Residential key on the desktop layout, then sign out. During the 520 ms AppRoot fade, the outgoing WideShell still rebuilds after the active membership is cleared. _Sidebar at wide_shell.dart:165 and _ConnectSection at wide_shell.dart:74 dereference activeMembership with a null assertion. Native Mac testing logged both errors and a secondary RenderFlex overflow. An isolated real-account widget test, live_logout_smoke_test.dart, reproduced the same sign-out failure without changing the OS proxy.</p><p>The Mac connection subchecks passed, but the overall Mac smoke suite failed because of these UI exceptions. Recommended fix: let the outgoing shell safely handle a cleared membership, or preserve its rendering data through the transition. No application code was changed.</p></div><div class="issue" style="margin-top:16px"><h3>High priority: no way to sign out when there is no usable plan</h3><p>Sign in with NO_PLANS, RES_INACTIVE or NON_GEO_PENDING. The app opens its membership gate, which contains purchase/renew actions but no Settings or sign-out control. A customer cannot replace their API key through the UI. This was reproduced in the real-account widget screens at all four sizes; the same AppRoot/PlansScreen gate also appears on native platforms.</p><p>The initial BOTH_ACTIVE chooser also lacks Settings until a plan is selected, but the user can escape that chooser by selecting an active plan. Recommended fix: expose Settings or a direct sign-out action on the membership gate.</p></div>
<h2>Account observations</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Fixture</th><th>Observed supported plans</th><th>Usable</th><th>ISP IPs</th><th>Account/layout</th></tr></thead><tbody>ROWS</tbody></table></div>
<p><b>ISP_INACTIVE is a mixed-state fixture:</b> the real backend provides one suspended plan and one still-usable expiring plan with four ISP IPs. Its account name is not evidence of a fully inactive backend state. BOTH_ACTIVE includes two usable plans and one expired ISP plan; unrelated historical products are filtered out.</p>
<p>Trial and paid Residential/ISP keys work through the same UI. Country Geo displays as a Country Geo plan. The Non-Geo key awaiting payment is mapped to Suspended and cannot connect; the UI uses normalized plan status rather than the backend’s payment wording. No exhaustive targeting or payment corner cases were attempted.</p>
<h2>Screenshot evidence</h2><p>Choose an account and size. Screenshots are embedded; this report works offline without a server.</p><select id="account"></select><select id="size"><option value="small-phone">Small phone · 320×568</option><option value="phone" selected>Phone · 393×852</option><option value="tablet">Tablet · 820×1180</option><option value="desktop">Desktop · 1440×900</option></select><img id="shot" alt="Real account screen">
<h2>Coverage and limits</h2><ul><li>40 existing API, controller, bypass, Dart proxy and Swift proxy regression tests passed. These use synthetic fixtures and are supporting regression evidence, separate from the real-account results.</li><li>Real account checks read account data and verify supported memberships, usable states, pool types, ISP assignments, initial screen rendering and controller sign-out. Native iOS additionally exercised real key entry, sign-out confirmation, plan switching, ISP selection and Residential country selection.</li><li>Only paid Residential and paid ISP were used for connection probes. Trial, Country Geo and inactive keys were display checks. No account plans were changed, keys revoked, traffic deliberately exhausted, or paid overage requested.</li><li>Physical iPhone/Android, native tablet compatibility, background recovery, broader OS/device coverage, separate Android browser routing, strict targeting and all error corner cases remain unverified. iOS VPN connection acceptance needs a physical device.</li><li>Android 16 booted but its ADB transport became unresponsive; Android 10 was used instead. Native builds were serialized after simultaneous builds conflicted in shared Flutter hook output. These are harness issues, not app test failures.</li><li>The native iOS screenshot tool failed; native navigation was verified from accessibility state. The gallery consists of widget-rendered evidence.</li></ul>
<h2>Reproducibility</h2><p><code>test/live_account_smoke_test.dart</code> reads a private JSON file via SHIFTER_QA_ACCOUNTS. <code>integration_test/real_account_smoke_test.dart</code> uses a private QA_ACCOUNTS define and the real native proxy engine with an in-memory store, preserving the Mac’s saved customer login/preferences. Raw keys, gateway passwords, personal account identifiers and exit addresses are excluded from this report.</p><p id="cleanup">CLEANUP</p>
<script>const images=IMAGES;const names=NAMES;const a=document.querySelector('#account'),s=document.querySelector('#size'),img=document.querySelector('#shot');names.forEach(n=>{const o=document.createElement('option');o.value=n;o.textContent=n;a.append(o)});function show(){img.src=images[a.value+'_'+s.value+'.png'];img.alt=a.value+' '+s.value}a.onchange=s.onchange=show;show();</script></main></html>'''
doc = doc.replace('CARDS', cards).replace('ROWS', rows).replace('IMAGES', json.dumps(images)).replace('NAMES', json.dumps([a['account'] for a in accounts]))
cleanup = (OUT / 'cleanup.txt').read_text() if (OUT / 'cleanup.txt').exists() else 'Cleanup verification pending.'
doc = doc.replace('CLEANUP', html.escape(cleanup))
(OUT / 'report.html').write_text(doc)
print('Self-contained report rendered.')
